  "domain": "governance",
  "definition": "Distributed team collaboration encompasses the practices, tools, and organisational patterns that enable geographically dispersed individuals working across multiple time zones to coordinate effectively on shared goals without co-location. It integrates asynchronous communication protocols, synchronous video conferencing, shared digital workspaces, version-controlled artefacts, and social norms around documentation and decision-making transparency to replicate \u2014 and often surpass \u2014 the coordination bandwidth of co-located teams. The discipline has grown from a niche practice of open-source communities and multinational corporations into a mainstream organisational capability following the global shift to remote work accelerated by the 2020 pandemic.",
